---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Alex Ainsworth: consumer product leader at Slingshot AI, previously Head of Product at Runna and first PM at Cleo AI. Also a former scuba instructor.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap intro">
      <div>
        <span class="mono">Product person · ex scuba instructor · part-time Dungeon Master</span>
        <h1>Hello, I'm Alex.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          I build consumer subscription apps, mostly ones with some AI under the hood and some good for the world on top. I've been the first PM at a fintech, led product at a running app through an acquisition, and now I'm working on an AI for mental health.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          The part I love is building for people who can't tell you what they want. That usually means a lot of time in the behavioural data until a pattern shows up, then shipping something and watching thousands of people get excited about it. I'm happiest close to the customer and moving fast, and I will argue about onboarding flows at dinner parties if you let me.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="intro-photo">
        <Photo />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Where I've worked</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="rows career">
        <li class="row">
          <span class="mono">2026 to now</span>
          <h3>Slingshot AI</h3>
          <p>Product Lead on Ash, the first AI designed for mental health, at the a16z-backed lab building it. I look after the consumer product end to end: how people find Ash, start using it, stick with it and decide it's worth paying for.</p>
          <span class="tag">Now</span>
        </li>
        <li class="row">
          <span class="mono">2024 to 2026</span>
          <h3>Runna</h3>
          <p>Joined as the second PM and finished as Head of Product, as we grew from around 100k subscribers to over a million. Launched Runna's first LLM feature, grew one team into eight, and turned a long slide in beginner retention back into growth.</p>
          <span class="tag">Acquired by Strava</span>
        </li>
        <li class="row">
          <span class="mono">2023 to 2024</span>
          <h3>Thirdfort</h3>
          <p>Senior PM for the consumer apps. Rebuilt the journey behind most of the company's revenue and led a scheme for sharing ID checks across the property market.</p>
          <span class="tag"></span>
        </li>
        <li class="row">
          <span class="mono">2022 to 2023</span>
          <h3>Utila, Honduras</h3>
          <p>Eighteen months travelling, a year of it teaching scuba diving. More on that below.</p>
          <span class="tag">Sabbatical</span>
        </li>
        <li class="row">
          <span class="mono">2019 to 2022</span>
          <h3>Cleo AI</h3>
          <p>The first PM. Built the React Native app and the subscription product behind what's now a $400m+ ARR business, then became Chief of Staff for Product ahead of the Series C.</p>
          <span class="tag">First PM</span>
        </li>
        <li class="row">
          <span class="mono">2018 to 2019</span>
          <h3>Theodo</h3>
          <p>PM and agile coach, shipping products for everyone from Series A startups to investment banks.</p>
          <span class="tag"></span>
        </li>
        <li class="row">
          <span class="mono">2013 to 2017</span>
          <h3>University of Exeter</h3>
          <p>First Class BSc (Hons) in Economics and Politics, with a placement year at IBM. My dissertation on income inequality and tax avoidance scored 79%.</p>
          <span class="tag">First Class</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap underwater">
      <div class="panel">
        <span class="mono">Utila, Honduras · <span class="accent">MSDT</span></span>
        <h2>The year I spent underwater</h2>
        <p>
          After Cleo AI's Series C, I did the sensible thing and took eighteen months off to travel. A year of it was spent on Utila, a small island off Honduras, teaching scuba diving: hundreds of students certified, from nervous first-timers to professional divemasters, and a lot of mornings spent on ocean clean-ups.
        </p>
        <p>
          It taught me more about product than I expected. Explaining something complicated, clearly, to someone who is slightly panicking is most of the job. So is staying calm when the kit breaks, the weather turns and a boat full of backpackers is looking at you for a plan.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Photo caption="Utila, about 18m down" ratio="4 / 5" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Off the clock</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="offclock">
        <div>
          <span class="mono">01</span>
          <h3>AI operating system</h3>
          <p>I run my personal life on a system I built in Claude Code. Either very efficient or a very elaborate way to procrastinate.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="mono">02</span>
          <h3>Dungeon Master</h3>
          <p>I run a Dungeons &amp; Dragons campaign. Excellent training for stakeholder management.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="mono">03</span>
          <h3>Chillies and hot sauce</h3>
          <p>I grow far too many chillies and turn them into hot sauce. Results vary. Mostly edible.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="mono">04</span>
          <h3>Tottenham Hotspur</h3>
          <p>A lifelong lesson in managing expectations.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="mono">05</span>
          <h3>Travel</h3>
          <p>Somewhere a little unexpected, ideally. Favourites so far: Cuba, Japan, Ukraine and Northern Iraq.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .intro h1 {
    margin: 1rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .intro-photo {
    max-width: 24rem;
    width: 100%;
    justify-self: end;
  }

  .underwater {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .underwater .panel {
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .underwater h2 {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .underwater p + p {
    margin-top: 1em;
  }

  .offclock {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(13rem, 1fr));
  }

  .offclock > div {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.75rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
  }

  .offclock h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .offclock p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .intro,
    .underwater {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .intro-photo {
      justify-self: start;
      max-width: 16rem;
      order: -1;
    }
  }
</style>
